# Docker build-context boundary (Sprint 23, ORG-PR-001).
#
# Both production Dockerfiles (apps/api/Dockerfile, apps/web-demo/Dockerfile)
# build from the repository root so `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` sees the
# whole workspace. This file keeps that context small, deterministic, and
# secret-safe: nothing listed here may ever influence a production artifact.
# The artifact smoke test (tooling/artifact-smoke.sh) independently asserts
# that none of this material reaches the built images.

# Version control and repository metadata.
.git
.github

# Environment files. Real or local secrets must NEVER enter a build context;
# runtime configuration is injected only when a container starts.
# (`**/` prefixes matter: without them Docker matches only at the context root.)
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the build stage from pnpm-lock.yaml.
**/node_modules
**/.pnpm-store

# Build outputs — always rebuilt inside the build stage.
**/dist
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage

# Logs, scanner output, local databases, temp files.
**/*.log
**/*.sarif
**/*.sqlite
**/*.output

# Local assistant/tooling state (mirrors .gitignore).
.claude
.tokensave

# Editor / OS metadata.
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode

# Local infrastructure and CI definitions — not part of any image.
infra
docs
tooling
**/*.md
LICENSE
